
## Database (PostgreSQL)

- Start it: `docker compose up -d db` (port 5452), then `cp .env.example .env`
  once — the app and `spider migrate` read `PG_HOST`, `PG_PORT`, `PG_USER`,
  `PG_PASSWORD`, `PG_DB` from `.env`.
- Queries: `spider.pg.query(T, c.arena, "SELECT ... WHERE id = $1", .{id})`,
  `queryOne` → `?T`, `queryExecute(void, arena, sql)`. Struct fields map to
  column names; a missing column or a NULL into a non-optional field is an
  error — use `?T` for nullable columns.
- Transactions: `var tx = try spider.pg.begin(); defer tx.rollback(); ...;
  try tx.commit();` — never `query(void, .., "BEGIN")` (refused: each call
  runs on its own pooled connection).
- Migrations: `src/core/db/migrations/<timestamp>_<name>.sql` with
  `-- migrate:up` / `-- migrate:down` sections, listed in
  `src/core/db/migrations.zig`. `spider g feature` creates one; apply it with
  `spider migrate`, then restart the app. **Until you do, the feature's pages
  answer 500**; the log shows `relation "<table>" does not exist`.
